{
  "id": "2CH.35",
  "number": "35",
  "bookId": "2CH",
  "reference": "2 Chronicles 35",
  "verseCount": 27,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "35",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2CH 35"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "35",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "King Josiah celebrated the Passover at Jerusalem in honour of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "; on the fourteenth day of the first month they killed the animals for the festival. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He assigned to the priests the duties they were to perform in the Temple and encouraged them to do them well. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He also gave these instructions to the Levites, the teachers of Israel, who were dedicated to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ": “Put the sacred Covenant Box in the Temple that King Solomon, the son of David, built. You are no longer to carry it from place to place, but you are to serve the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God and his people Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "2CH.8.14"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "2 Chr 8.14",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Take your places in the Temple by clans, according to the responsibilities assigned to you by King David and his son King Solomon, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and arrange yourselves so that some of you will be available to help each family of the people of Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You are to kill the Passover lambs and goats. Now make yourselves ritually clean and prepare the sacrifices in order that your fellow-Israelites may follow the instructions which the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " gave through Moses.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the use of the people at the Passover, King Josiah contributed from his own herds and flocks 30,000 sheep, lambs, and young goats, and 3,000 bulls. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "His officials also made contributions for the people, the priests, and the Levites to use. And the officials in charge of the Temple — Hilkiah, the High Priest, Zechariah, and Jehiel — gave the priests 2,600 lambs and young goats and 300 bulls for sacrifices during the festival. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The leaders of the Levites — Conaniah, Shemaiah and his brother Nethanel, Hashabiah, Jeiel, and Jozabad — contributed 5,000 lambs and young goats and 500 bulls for the Levites to offer as sacrifices.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When everything was arranged for the Passover, the priests and the Levites took their places, as commanded by the king. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the lambs and goats had been killed, the Levites skinned them, and the priests sprinkled the blood on the altar. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then they divided among the people, by family groups, the animals for burnt offerings, so that they could offer them according to the instructions in the Law of Moses. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EXO.12.8+EXO.12.9"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ex 12.8–9",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Levites roasted the Passover sacrifices over the fire, according to the regulations, and boiled the sacred offerings in pots, cauldrons, and pans, and quickly distributed the meat to the people. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After this was done, the Levites provided meat for themselves and for the priests descended from Aaron, for the priests were kept busy until night, burning the animals that were burnt whole and the fat of the sacrifices. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1CH.25.1"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Chr 25.1",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The following musicians of the Levite clan of Asaph were in the places assigned to them by King David's instructions: Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun, the king's prophet. The guards at the temple gates did not need to leave their posts, because the other Levites prepared the Passover for them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So, as King Josiah had commanded, everything was done that day for the worship of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the keeping of the Passover Festival, and the offering of burnt offerings on the altar. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EXO.12.1+EXO.12.2+EXO.12.3+EXO.12.4+EXO.12.5+EXO.12.6+EXO.12.7+EXO.12.8+EXO.12.9+EXO.12.10+EXO.12.11+EXO.12.12+EXO.12.13+EXO.12.14+EXO.12.15+EXO.12.16+EXO.12.17+EXO.12.18+EXO.12.19+EXO.12.20"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ex 12.1–20",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For seven days all the people of Israel who were present celebrated the Passover and the Festival of Unleavened Bread. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Since the days of the prophet Samuel, the Passover had never been celebrated like this. None of the former kings had ever celebrated a Passover like this one celebrated by King Josiah, the priests, the Levites, and the people of Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "in the eighteenth year of Josiah's reign.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After King Josiah had done all this for the Temple, King Neco of Egypt led an army to fight at Carchemish on the River Euphrates. Josiah tried to stop him, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but Neco sent Josiah this message: “This war I am fighting does not concern you, King of Judah. I have not come to fight you, but to fight my enemies, and God has told me to hurry. God is on my side, so don't oppose me, or he will destroy you.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Josiah was determined to fight. He refused to listen to what God was saying through King Neco, so he disguised himself and went into battle on the plain of Megiddo.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "During the battle King Josiah was struck by Egyptian arrows. He ordered his servants, “Take me away; I'm badly hurt!” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They lifted him out of his chariot, placed him in a second chariot which he had there, and took him to Jerusalem. There he died and was buried in the royal tombs. All the people of Judah and Jerusalem mourned his death.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.24"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The prophet Jeremiah composed a lament for King Josiah. It has become a custom in Israel for the singers, both men and women, to use this song when they mourn for him. The song is found in the collection of laments.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.35.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.35.25"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 35:25"
          },
          "items": [
